CVM1|A|F
E|FIX A verified: the system branch now sits after the failure detection; a system record with no failure signal still reads 'session init'/Noise, and one carrying is_error reads Failed
E|FIX B verified: a private case-insensitive TryGetProperty replaces every JsonElement.TryGetProperty call site in the file, matching AgentOutputObserver.FindString
E|FIX C verified: the failed tool_result branch still returns immediately while other branches only set 'first', so a failure in any block beats an earlier text block and the no-failure case is unchanged
E|FIX D partially verified: exit_code and aggregated_output are read, malformed and absent values fall back safely, and the × marker is one already used in this file so no new glyph is introduced
E|Only LogLine.cs and the self-tests changed; no using-alias was added
T|dotnet build FKNRTD.CLI.sln -c Release => 0 warnings, 0 errors (auditor)
T|dotnet run --project tests/FKNRTD.SelfTest -c Release --no-build => 117/117 self-tests passed (auditor)
B|FIX D changed the SUCCESS case, which the brief did not ask for, and made the commonest line in the log worse. A command that exits 0 now renders '> exit 0: dotnet build - first second' instead of '> dotnet build', and the whole aggregated output is appended to it. Your own new self-test asserts this: (code == 0 ? "> " : "× ") + $"exit {code}: dotnet build - first second". Nearly every command in a real Codex log completes successfully and carries exit_code 0, so in practice every command row now begins with a redundant 'exit 0:' and is filled with that command's output instead of naming the command. Success is the unmarked default in this file - nothing else annotates it - and the log view exists to be read at a glance. Restore the success rendering to exactly '> ' + Clip(command), unchanged from before, and keep the new '× exit N: command - output' form for a non-zero exit only. Update the self-test to assert the success case is byte-identical to the old behaviour.
